  "text": "The influence of a range of dissolved salts and organic molecules on how water molecules connect to each other was examined by tracking the tiny changes in the magnetic signal of the hydrogen atoms in water. To isolate the effect of the dissolved substances, the overall magnetic response of the solution was adjusted using a known reference signal from a simple organic liquid. After this correction, the shifts in the water signal were recorded for many different solutes. The results show how various dissolved compounds modify the hydrogen‑bond network of water, providing insight into the way water’s structure changes in the presence of different chemical species."
